<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch April cash retail sales rise 2.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch April cash retail sales rise 2.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail sales rose 2.7 percent in cash terms in April compared with April 1996, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>In volume terms April retail sales were also 2.7 percent higher than in April 1996, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES		   April 97   March 97   April 96</p>
<p> Pct change cash yr/yr		   2.7	  3.5	  4.1</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   106	  105	  103</p>
<p> Pct change prices yr/yr		 0.0	 -0.1	  0.0</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   101	  101	  101</p>
<p> Pct change volume yr/yr		 2.7	  3.6	  4.0</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   104	  104	  102</p>
<p>NOTES - The CBS noted that April 1997 had one Monday less and one Wednesday more than April 1996. It said April retail sales might also have been influenced by the fact that Easter fell in March this year and in April last year.  </p>
<p> DUTCH RETAIL SALES IN DETAIL    April 97   March 97  Jan-Apr 97</p>
<p>						   (pct changes yr/yr)</p>
<p> Food cash				   2.9	  0.9	  3.2</p>
<p> Food prices				 0.0	 -0.5	  0.6</p>
<p> Food volume				 3.0	  1.4	  2.6</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food cash	 3.1	  6.7	  5.3</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food prices     0.0	  0.2	 -0.1</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food volume     3.2	  6.5	  5.5</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
